 for ttfx to exit before it finishes.","fretish":"when user_lock_requested & ttfx_running the system_lock shall eventually satisfy ttfx_signalled & ttfx_wait_bounded"},"candidate":{"description":"When the user locks the session and ttfx is running, omarchy-system-lock shall send SIGTERM to ttfx after the shell reports the lock secure. The script shall wait up to 1 s for ttfx to exit before it finishes. A lock that is not secure leaves the screensaver running.","fretish":"when user_lock_requested & lock_secure_reported & ttfx_running the system_lock shall eventually satisfy ttfx_signalled & ttfx_wait_bounded"}},"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-260912-MXQG","parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP"],"title":"When the user locks the session and ttfx is running, omarchy-system-lock shall send SIGTERM to ttfx after the shell reports the lock secure. The script shall wait up to 1 s for ttfx to exit before it finishes. A lock that is not secure leaves the screensaver running."},{"changeStatus":"added","changedFields":["status","priority","category","req_type","fretish","description","formalization_strategy","parent","component","rationale","variables","traces.satisfies","verification.assurance_level","verification.formalization_status"],"clause":{"candidate":{"description":"When the user locks the session, omarchy-system-lock shall exit 0 only after the shell reports this lock request secure. The script shall exit 1 when the shell refuses or cannot track the request. It shall also exit 1 when the shell ends the request before it is secure, or does not secure it within 10 s. On exit 1 it shall also send the critical \"Screen did not lock\" notification.","fretish":"when user_lock_requested the system_lock shall eventually satisfy (lock_exit_success <=> lock_secure_reported) & (lock_failure_notified <=> !lock_secure_reported)"}},"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-261006-861H","parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP"],"title":"When the user locks the session, omarchy-system-lock shall exit 0 only after the shell reports this lock request secure. The script shall exit 1 when the shell refuses or cannot track the request. It shall also exit 1 when the shell ends the request before it is secure, or does not secure it within 10 s. On exit 1 it shall also send the critical \"Screen did not lock\" notification."},{"changeStatus":"added","changedFields":["status","priority","category","req_type","fretish","description","formalization_strategy","parent","component","rationale","variables","traces.satisfies","verification.assurance_level","verification.formalization_status"],"clause":{"candidate":{"description":"When a caller reads the outcome of a tracked lock request, the lock service shall report it secured only if that request became secure. Only a request from this shell instance can read secured. The service shall keep a secured outcome readable for 30 s after the request ends, also when the user unlocks at once. Another request, a request from an earlier shell instance, and an expired request shall not read secured.","fretish":"when lock_result_read the lock_service shall always satisfy lock_receipt_secured <=> (lock_request_secured & !lock_receipt_expired)"}},"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-261009-RCPT","parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP"],"title":"When a caller reads the outcome of a tracked lock request, the lock service shall report it secured only if that request became secure. Only a request from this shell instance can read secured. The service shall keep a secured outcome readable for 30 s after the request ends, also when the user unlocks at once. Another request, a request from an earlier shell instance, and an expired request shall not read secured."},{"changeStatus":"modified","changedFields":["description"],"clause":{"base":{"description":"When the user locks the session, the system shall engage the session lock through the shell IPC. The system shall reset the keyboard layout to the default. The system shall stop the ttfx screensaver and wait for it to exit before closing its terminal. The system shall lock 1Password when it is running.","fretish":"when user_lock_requested the lock_component shall eventually satisfy session_lock_engaged & keyboard_layout_default & screensaver_stopped"},"candidate":{"description":"When the user locks the session, the system shall engage the session lock through the shell IPC. The system shall reset the keyboard layout to the default. Once the session lock is secure, the system shall stop the ttfx screensaver and wait for it to exit before closing its terminal. The system shall lock 1Password when it is running.","fretish":"when user_lock_requested the lock_component shall eventually satisfy session_lock_engaged & keyboard_layout_default & screensaver_stopped"}},"component":"lock","id":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","parent":"STK-REQ-260912-XJ5D","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260912-XJ5D"],"title":"When the user locks the session, the system shall engage the session lock through the shell IPC. The system shall reset the keyboard layout to the default. Once the session lock is secure, the system shall stop the ttfx screensaver and wait for it to exit before closing its terminal. The system shall lock 1Password when it is running."},{"changeStatus":"modified","changedFields":["description"],"clause":{"base":{"description":"The menu Lock row invokes the lock component's CLI entry point omarchy-system-lock with no arguments. The callee engages the session lock and exits 0. This is the only menu-to-lock interaction; lock never calls menu.","fretish":"when lock_row_activated the menu shall eventually satisfy system_lock_invoked"},"candidate":{"description":"The menu Lock row invokes the lock component's CLI entry point omarchy-system-lock with no arguments. The callee exits 0 once the session lock is secure. When the lock does not hold, it exits 1 and shows a notification (SW-REQ-261006-861H). This is the only menu-to-lock interaction; lock never calls menu.","fretish":"when lock_row_activated the menu shall eventually satisfy system_lock_invoked"}},"component":"menu","id":"SYS-REQ-260927-WC89","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260912-XJ5D"],"title":"The menu Lock row invokes the lock component's CLI entry point omarchy-system-lock with no arguments. The callee exits 0 once the session lock is secure. When the lock does not hold, it exits 1 and shows a notification (SW-REQ-261006-861H). This is the only menu-to-lock interaction; lock never calls menu."}],"intentEdits":5,"sources":["changeRequest.body","changeRequest.title","requirement:SW-REQ-260912-MXQG","requirement:SW-REQ-261006-861H","requirement:SW-REQ-261009-RCPT","requirement:SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","requirement:SYS-REQ-260927-WC89"],"status":"declared","title":"Confirm each lock request became secure before reporting success"},"nextDecision":{"disclosureIds":["compat_change_unapproved:cf-d8ef7288e46a310a"],"kind":"human_judgement","question":"Approve each of the 1 backward-compatibility change: a reviewer or above approves it, or the author fixes it.","reason":"compat_changes_unapproved"},"preservedBehaviour":{"requirements":[{"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-260912-J8SX","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP"],"title":"When the lock IPC handler receives a lock request and /etc/pam.d/omarchy-lock-password is missing, the lock service shall answer missing-pam. It shall not engage the session lock."},{"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-260912-ND55","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP"],"title":"When the idle blank timer expires during a locked session, the lock service shall blank the displays only when no password authentication is in flight. The armed fingerprint PAM shall not hold the display lit. When wall-clock time shows the timer froze through a suspend, the service shall re-arm the timer instead of blanking."},{"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-260912-WJYM","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["error_handling"],"parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-FRG0","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-FRG0"],"title":"When the stranded-lock probe exits 0, the service holds no lock, and password PAM exists, the lock service shall take the session lock once. It shall log a lock-stranded recovery event."},{"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-261004-296X","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP"],"title":"The lock service shall report the reader unavailable after 3 probe answers in a row that are neither a listed print nor a definite none. When the service treats fingerprint authentication as configured, 3 unusable attempts in a row shall also cause the report. A usable attempt shows a finger prompt and does not end in a device error within 2 s of the prompt. An attempt that shows a prompt clears the report. After a usable attempt, the service shall start the next attempt after 250 ms. After n unusable attempts, it shall wait 1 s times 2 to the power n-1, at most 40 s. It shall abort an attempt that shows no prompt within 20 s. It shall count a miss within 5 s after a resume as the first miss. It shall restart an attempt or a wait that spans a suspend within 250 ms. User activity shall shorten a longer wait to 250 ms. It shall do so at most once per 2 s or once per current wait, whichever is longer. At the 40 s cap, it shall do so only 32 s after the last attempt ended."},{"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-261004-V813","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP"],"title":"When the lock screen's enrollment probe finishes, the lock service shall classify the answer. It shall treat fingerprint authentication as configured when the answer lists an enrolled fingerprint. It shall treat it as not configured when the answer says that the user has none. The same applies when the fingerprint PAM file or fprintd-list is missing. Any other answer shall leave the state unchanged, for example when the service cannot reach fprintd. While fingerprint authentication stays unconfigured after such an answer, the service shall run the probe again after the attempt backoff."},{"component":"lock","id":"SW-REQ-261004-VVN2","matchLevel":"file","parent":"SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["SYS-REQ-260912-T0XP"],"title":"The lock view's password field shall consume an auto-repeated key press without editing the text, except for Backspace and Delete. A key held while a blanked display wakes then cannot fill the field with one character."},{"component":"lock","id":"SYS-REQ-260912-FRG0","matchLevel":"file","obligations":["error_handling"],"parent":"STK-REQ-260912-XJ5D","relation":"code_changed","satisfies":["STK-REQ-260912-XJ5D"],"title":"The system shall report the compositor session-lock state as an exit code. Exit 0 means some monitor reports LOCK blocking it. Exit 1 means a monitor answered and none shows LOCK. Exit 2 means the probes cannot determine the state. When the shell detects a stranded lock left by a dead client and password PAM exists, the shell shall take the lock once. It shall record the recovery in the journal."}],"total":7},"readiness":"not_assessed","requiredAuthority":{"acceptedIdentitySources":["github_login","portal_user"],"basis":"approved_policy","enforcement":"portal_or_forge","policyDigest":"sha256:19ad4c0c6f4aa212c59917968707493bbf687a2badfa6754165c7cf20f03d281","policyRevision":"1e43373287afbd6dca4674ad463d5b5db7812358","role":"reviewer"},"routineEvidence":{"claimsObservedPass":8,"gatesAdvisory":28,"gatesNotApplicable":1,"gatesPassed":177,"testsPassed":14},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.decision-summary.v1","scope":{"approximations":["Function-level mapping comes from trace targets `path:symbol` / line ranges (authored + derived) and function-local annotation